# Git status gates (before work and before commit/PR)

Do not assume the previous chat’s branch, PR, or working tree is still valid. Re-check.

## Gate 1 — before any edits or mutating commands

Read-only first, together:

1. `git status -sb` — dirty vs clean, ahead/behind, merge/rebase
2. `git branch --show-current` — never treat `develop`/`main` as a feature branch
3. `git fetch origin develop` when starting work or opening a PR
4. `git log origin/develop -12 --oneline` and `git log -8 --oneline` — what already landed vs this branch
5. Open PR for this branch: `gh pr view --json state,mergedAt,url` or `gh pr list --head <branch>`

If already on a feature branch: `git log origin/develop..HEAD --oneline` and `git diff --stat origin/develop...HEAD`.

**Do not start implementing** until you know: current branch, whether the request is already on `develop` or in an open/merged PR, and which files are already dirty.

| State | Action |
|-------|--------|
| Dirty tree unrelated to the request | Do not mix work; leave those files alone |
| Merge/rebase in progress | Finish or abort that first |
| On `develop` or `main` | Branch from up-to-date `develop` before editing |
| Feature branch whose PR is **MERGED** | Switch to up-to-date `develop`; do not pull `develop` into the dead branch |
| Requested work already on `develop` | Do not re-implement; say so |
| Unrelated open PR on the current branch | New branch from `develop`; do not pile unrelated commits onto that PR |

## Gate 2 — after work, before commit and before `gh pr create`

Run again (do not reuse Gate 1 output):

1. `git status -sb` — only intended files; no `.env`, credentials, or unrelated dirt
2. `git diff` and `git diff --stat` — staged + unstaged match the request
3. `git log origin/develop..HEAD --oneline` — commits that will enter the PR
4. `git diff --stat origin/develop...HEAD` — full PR scope, not only the last commit

Then commit (see `git-workflow.mdc` + `no-ai-commit-attribution.mdc`). After commit, `git status` and `git log -1 --format=%B` (no AI trailers). Before opening or updating the PR, repeat the `origin/develop...HEAD` log/diff so the Summary matches **all** commits, not just the latest.

## Do not

- Skip these gates because the last turn already ran git
- Commit or open a PR without Gate 2
- Pull `develop` into a merged feature branch to “sync”
